solution:
Vanita will visit exactly one of the eight sites she knows, so each site is one possibility.

S = {Ajintha, Mahabaleshwar, Lonar Sarovar, Tadoba wild life sanctuary, Amboli, Raigad, Matheran, Anandavan}

There are 8 possibilities, i.e. n(S) = 8.

A week has seven days, and exactly one of them is selected.

S = {Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday, Saturday, Sunday}

There are 7 possibilities, i.e. n(S) = 7.

The die can show any of 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6 and the coin can show H or T, and the two happen together, so every die result pairs with each coin result.

S = {1H, 1T, 2H, 2T, 3H, 3T, 4H, 4T, 5H, 5T, 6H, 6T}

\(n(S) = 6 \times 2 = 12\)

A two digit number is formed by choosing a tens digit and then a units digit from 2, 3 and 5, with no digit repeated. There are 3 choices for the tens place and 2 remaining choices for the units place.

S = {23, 25, 32, 35, 52, 53}

\(n(S) = 3 \times 2 = 6\)

The arrow can come to rest on any one of the six coloured sectors of the disc, so the colours themselves are the outcomes.

S = {Red, Purple, Orange, Yellow, Blue, Green}

n(S) = 6
